.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.remember/
eval/dataset.json
eval/results.json
provisioning/*.key
provisioning/tskey*

# Site-specific deployment detail: IPs, hostnames, physical layout.
# Operationally necessary on the coordinator, but not part of the published
# project. Every agent should READ it; nobody should commit it.
network.md
llama.log

# Agent worktrees and local Claude state. Never commit: the worktrees are
# embedded git repos and committing gitlinks pollutes the repo and confuses merges.
# Ignore the CONTENTS of .claude/, not the directory itself, so the two files
# that are project policy rather than local state can be tracked. The agent
# hardening hooks (docs/AGENT-HARDENING.md) are worthless if they only exist in
# one checkout -- they have to travel with the repo, and later into the Skill.
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/hooks/
.claude/hook-audit.log

# Benchmark output. Gitignored because the corpus files embed the OPERATOR'S
# REAL DOCUMENT TEXT -- chunk text and summaries of actual sensitive material --
# and this repository is published. The measurements derived from these runs
# belong in docs/measurements.md; the raw content must never leave the box.
bench/out/
